# CLAUDE.md — biquad-fit

> **Project map:** `.claude/MAP.md` — consult before starting any session.

## What This Is

**biquad-rust** is a Rust library that computes optimal parametric EQ (PEQ) filter parameters to match a measured frequency response to a target curve. Reverse-engineered from [jaakkopasanen/AutoEq](https://github.com/jaakkopasanen/AutoEq)

It does **not** apply EQ to audio. It computes filter parameters only.

Full technical spec: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`

---

## Development Approach

**TDD strictly.** Tests are written before or alongside implementation. A feature is not done until its tests pass.

**AutoEQ is the oracle.** Correctness is defined as: given the same inputs, produce outputs within 0.5 dB RMSE of what AutoEQ produces. Golden files in `tests/fixtures/golden/` are generated by running AutoEQ (Python) on the test fixtures.

## Current Status


**Test matrix:** 5 IEMs × 6 targets × 3 constraint sets = 90 combinations

IEM fixtures: `blessing3`, `hexa`, `andromeda`, `zero2`, `origin_s`

Target fixtures: `harman_ie_2019`, `diffuse_field`, `flat`, `v_shaped`, `bass_heavy`, `bright`

Constraint sets:
- **Standard:** 5 filters, gain ±12 dB, Q 0.5–10, LSQ + PK×3 + HSQ
- **Restricted:** 3 filters, gain ±6 dB, Q 1.0–5.0, PK only
- **Qudelix-10:** 10 filters, gain ±12 dB, Q 0.5–10, LSQ + PK×8 + HSQ
